  "summary": "Advocacy groups rallied in San Jose calling for Police Chief Paul Joseph's resignation and cancellation of the city's Flock Safety contract after an SJPD officer was fired for using ALPR data to help a relative stalk a woman. The City Council's Rules Committee advanced two proposals to tighten controls on ALPR access and expand audits, while advocates demand ending the Flock contract entirely.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Community advocates are calling for San Jose's police chief to step down, after revelations that a police officer used license plate tracking technology to help his cousin stalk a woman she alleges abused her.",
      "paragraph_idx": 3
    },
    {
      "quote": "our audits have shown that our license plate reader data has not gone anywhere it isn't supposed to go.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "The city's reliance on these cameras creates new threats, and there's no amount of safeguards that can truly eliminate the possibility of abuse",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    }
  ],
